.TH OYAMA-HRT-CLI 1 "2026-11-01" "Oyama's HRT Tracker 0.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oyama-hrt-cli \- command-line interface for Oyama's HRT Tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oyama-hrt-cli
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oyama-hrt-cli
is the command-line companion to
.BR oyama-hrt-app .
It manages the encrypted vault, PostgreSQL cluster, backups, and data
migration without the graphical interface.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print the application version.
.TP
.B vault setup
Initialize a new encrypted vault with a recovery phrase.
.TP
.B vault unlock \fB--phrase-stdin\fR
Unlock the vault using a recovery phrase read from stdin.
.TP
.B backup export \fIFILE\fR
Export an encrypted backup to \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B backup export --plaintext \fIFILE\fR
Export a plaintext (unencrypted) backup to \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B backup import \fIFILE\fR
Import a backup from \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B backup preview \fIFILE\fR
Preview the contents of a backup without importing.
.TP
.B db start
Start the managed PostgreSQL cluster.
.TP
.B db stop
Stop the managed PostgreSQL cluster.
.TP
.B db migrate-vault
Migrate a legacy plaintext database to the encrypted vault.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-phrase-stdin
Read the recovery phrase from stdin (disables terminal echo).
.TP
.B \-\-db \fINAME\fR
Specify the database name.
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIHOST\fR
Specify the PostgreSQL host.
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
Specify the PostgreSQL port.
.SH SECURITY
The CLI disables core dumps and marks itself non-dumpable before handling
vault secrets, to prevent recovery phrase leakage via core files.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/oyama-hrt/
Application configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oyama-hrt-app (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Oyama's HRT Tracker contributors.
